 </div>
 <div className="team-card__body">
 <p><strong>Responsibility:</strong> Badge preparation</p>
 <p>
 Prepare visitor badges, verify identification requirements, and set up
 access credentials for the zones included in the visit.
 </p>
 </div>
 </div>
 <div className="team-card">
 <div className="team-card__header team-card__header--ehs">
 <span className="team-card__icon" aria-hidden="true">⚠️</span>
 <span className="team-card__name">EHS</span>
 </div>
 <div className="team-card__body">
 <p><strong>Responsibility:</strong> Safety briefing</p>
 <p>
 Prepare safety briefing materials for the specific zones being visited,
 ensure PPE availability, and schedule the safety orientation.
 </p>
 </div>
 </div>
 <div className="team-card">
 <div className="team-card__header team-card__header--operations">
 <span className="team-card__icon" aria-hidden="true">🏭</span>
 <span className="team-card__name">Operations</span>
 </div>
 <div className="team-card__body">
 <p><strong>Responsibility:</strong> Tour guide assignment</p>
 <p>
 Assign a tour guide, plan the visitor route through production zones,
 and coordinate with the production schedule to minimize disruption.
 </p>
 </div>
 </div>
 </div>

 <h3 className="guide-section__subtitle">How Tasks Are Created</h3>
 <ol className="step-list">
 <li className="step-list__item">
 <span className="step-list__action">⚙ System Automatic</span>
 <p>
 When a visit request moves to <strong>Approved</strong> state, the system
 automatically creates fulfillment tasks for each team. Each task is linked to
 the visit request and includes a description of what needs to be done.
 </p>
 </li>
 <li className="step-list__item">
 <span className="step-list__action">⚙ System Automatic</span>
 <p>
 Each new task starts in <strong>Pending</strong> state and is categorized by
 team type (Security, EHS, or Operations).
 </p>
 </li>
 </ol>

 <h3 className="guide-section__subtitle">Working on Your Tasks</h3>
 <ol className="step-list">
 <li className="step-list__item">
 <span className="step-list__action">👤 Your Action</span>
 <p>
 Navigate to <strong>VoltWorks Plant Operations → Fulfillment → My Open Tasks</strong>
 to see all tasks assigned to you. This list filters to your tasks automatically
 and excludes any completed or cancelled tasks.
 </p>
 </li>
 <li className="step-list__item">
 <span className="step-list__action">👤 Your Action</span>
 <p>
 Open a task to see its details — the linked visit request, task description,
 and team type. Change the state to <strong>In Progress</strong> when you
 start working on it.
 </p>
 </li>
 <li className="step-list__item">
 <span className="step-list__action">👤 Your Action</span>
 <p>
 Once you have completed the preparation work, change the state to{" "}
 <strong>Completed</strong> and save the record.
 </p>
 </li>
 </ol>

 <h3 className="guide-section__subtitle">Task States</h3>
 <div className="state-flow">
 <span className="state-badge state-badge--pending">Pending</span>
 <span className="flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
 <span className="state-badge state-badge--in-progress">In Progress</span>
 <span className="flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
 <span className="state-badge state-badge--completed">Completed</span>
 </div>
 <p className="state-note">
 Tasks can also be set to <strong>Cancelled</strong> if the associated visit is
 cancelled.
 </p>

 <div className="callout callout--info">
 <strong>For Supervisors:</strong> You can monitor all team queues from the
 navigation menu — use <strong>Security Queue</strong>, <strong>EHS Queue</strong>,
 or <strong>Operations Queue</strong> under Fulfillment to see open tasks for each
 team. The <strong>All Open Tasks</strong> view shows everything across all teams.
 </div>
 </section>
 );
}
